  "plain": "A scientist named Filippo Biondi, who says he scanned beneath the pyramids of Giza in Egypt, reports that in 2025 his team found a tangle of signals in their underground images, the kind of pictures built up from waves bounced off hidden layers. He says it looks like a network of underground tunnels under the plateau, work he did alongside Armando Mei. If true, it would mean far more lies under the pyramids than anyone has mapped."
